Package: surface-camera
Version: 3.0
Section: graphics
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3, python3-gi, python3-pyqt6, python3-pyqt6.qtquick,
 python3-pyqt6.qtmultimedia, qml6-module-org-kde-kirigami,
 qml6-module-qtmultimedia, qml6-module-qtquick-controls,
 qml6-module-qtquick-layouts, gstreamer1.0-libcamera,
 gstreamer1.0-plugins-base, gstreamer1.0-plugins-good, libcamera-ipa,
 python3-numpy, python3-pil
Recommends: python3-zxing-cpp
Maintainer: chikara-linux <320610001+chikara-linux@users.noreply.github.com>
Description: Camera app for the Surface Go 2 IPU3 camera
 A touch friendly Kirigami camera application that talks to libcamera
 directly through GStreamer's libcamerasrc, instead of going through
 PipeWire.
 .
 On this hardware the PipeWire camera node only advertises up to
 1280x720, while the sensors can be driven at 2560x1920. Using
 libcamerasrc directly makes the full 5 megapixels available, and also
 reaches the rear camera that is deliberately hidden from PipeWire.
 .
 Photos are written to the Camera folder inside the user's Pictures
 directory. QR decoding uses python3-zxing-cpp.
